{:id :chart
 :title "Chart"
 :summary "Charts for a dashboard without a charting library: a time series as a line over a fading area with a comparison line and a crosshair, ranked rows with a rail under each label, a donut for shares and a sparkline for the trend beside a number."
 :category :data
 :group "Numbers"
 :keywords ["chart" "graph" "area chart" "line chart" "time series" "crosshair" "bar list" "ranking" "donut" "pie" "sparkline" "trend" "analytics" "dashboard" "legend"]

 :when-to-use
 ["One measure over days, weeks or hours, optionally against the period before: area-chart."
  "The top entries of a list by one number (pages, sources, countries): bar-list."
  "How a total splits into two to six parts: donut."
  "The recent course of a number, beside it in a metric: sparkline."]

 :when-not-to-use
 ["Use metric alone when the number matters and its course does not."
  "Use progress for one value against a known total."
  "Use day-grid for a yes or no record per day."
  "Use table when rows carry several numbers; a bar-list shows one."
  "For more than about 120 points, or several series with their own scales, bucket the data first (weeks instead of days) or use a charting library."]

 :usage "(require '[ui.chart :as chart]\n         '[ui.card :as card])\n\n(card/card {}\n  (chart/chart {:title \"Visitors\"\n                :description \"112 in the last 30 days, +19% on the 30 before\"}\n    (chart/area-chart\n      {:label \"This period\"\n       :compare-label \"Period before\"\n       :points [{:label \"Mon 16 Nov\" :value 3 :compare 1}\n                {:label \"Tue 17 Nov\" :value 1 :compare 4}\n                {:label \"Wed 18 Nov\" :value 5 :compare 2}]})))"

 :examples
 [{:title "Ranked rows that link to their detail"
   :code "(chart/bar-list\n  {:rows [{:label \"Blog\" :description \"/blog\" :value 48 :note \"12%\" :href \"/page?p=/blog\"}\n          {:label \"Notes\" :description \"/notes\" :value 27 :note \"7%\" :href \"/page?p=/notes\"}]})"}
  {:title "Shares of a whole"
   :code "(chart/donut\n  {:center-label \"visitors\"\n   :segments [{:label \"Direct\" :value 250}\n              {:label \"Search\" :value 27}\n              {:label \"Other sites\" :value 32}]})"}
  {:title "A sparkline in a metric"
   :code "(metric/metric {:label \"Visitors\" :value \"112\" :delta \"+19%\" :trend :up\n                :chart (chart/sparkline {:values [9 13 14 17 44 25 31 23 17 22 39 21 12]\n                                         :label \"Visitors per week, last 13 weeks\"})})"}]

 :api
 [{:fn "chart"
   :doc "The frame of a chart: an h3 title with an optional description on the left, actions on the right, then the children. It has no surface; put it in a card."
   :children "The chart and what belongs to it (a legend, a note)."
   :props [{:name :title :type "string | hiccup" :doc "What is charted."}
           {:name :description :type "string | hiccup" :doc "One line under the title: the total, the range, the change."}
           {:name :actions :type "hiccup" :doc "Controls at the right of the title row, usually a boxed button-group as the range picker."}
           {:name :class :type "string"} {:name :attrs :type "map"}]}
  {:fn "area-chart"
   :doc "A time series as a line over an area that fades to the baseline. With :compare values a dashed line of the comparison series is drawn behind it and a legend under it. Each point has a column over the plot: hovering or tapping it shows a crosshair, a dot per series and a card with the values. The plot is 200px high (--chart-h) and as wide as its container."
   :props [{:name :points :type "vector of point maps" :doc "Oldest first. Each map: :label (name in the value card, \"Thu 5 Nov\"), :value (number), :compare (optional number of the comparison series), :axis-label (optional, labels this point on the x axis; without any, about five evenly spaced points are labeled with :label)."}
           {:name :label :type "string" :default "\"Value\"" :doc "Name of the series in the card and the legend."}
           {:name :compare-label :type "string" :default "\"Before\"" :doc "Name of the comparison series."}
           {:name :color :type ":accent | :blue | :teal | :orange | :pink | :success" :default "the first series token" :doc "Color of the line, the area and the dots."}
           {:name :max :type "number" :default "nice-max of the data" :doc "Top of the value axis. Set it to give several charts the same scale."}
           {:name :curve :type ":smooth | :linear" :default ":smooth" :doc "Bent through the points without leaving the plot, or straight segments."}
           {:name :format :type "fn number -> string" :default "format-number" :doc "Text of a value on the axis and in the card."}
           {:name :legend :type "boolean" :default "true with a comparison series" :doc "false hides the legend."}
           {:name :loading :type "boolean" :default "false" :doc "A skeleton of the plot's size instead of the chart."}
           {:name :empty-label :type "string" :default "\"No data for this range\"" :doc "Shown in an empty-state when :points is empty."}
           {:name :class :type "string"} {:name :attrs :type "map"}]}
  {:fn "bar-list"
   :doc "Ranked rows: the label with its value at the end of the line and a 4px rail under them, filled to the row's share of the largest value. A row with :href is a link with a hover surface."
   :props [{:name :rows :type "vector of row maps" :doc "Largest first. Each map: :label, :description (muted, after the label), :value (number, sets the rail), :display (the value as shown), :note (muted, after the value, such as the share), :href, :active."}
           {:name :max :type "number" :default "the largest :value" :doc "Value of a full rail."}
           {:name :color :type ":accent | :blue | :teal | :orange | :pink | :success" :default "the first series token" :doc "Color of the rails."}
           {:name :class :type "string"} {:name :attrs :type "map"}]}
  {:fn "donut"
   :doc "Shares of a whole as a 144px ring with a number in the middle and a legend beside it (under it when there is no room): name, value and share per segment. Segments are colored in order: the four series tokens, then two neutrals."
   :props [{:name :segments :type "vector of segment maps" :doc "Largest first, at most six. Each map: :label, :value (number), :display (the value as shown), :active (thicker segment, bolder legend row)."}
           {:name :center-value :type "string | hiccup" :default "the total" :doc "The number in the middle."}
           {:name :center-label :type "string" :doc "A line under it, such as the unit."}
           {:name :format :type "fn number -> string" :default "format-number" :doc "Text of a value."}
           {:name :legend :type "boolean" :default "true" :doc "false leaves the legend out."}
           {:name :class :type "string"} {:name :attrs :type "map"}]}
  {:fn "sparkline"
   :doc "A 104 by 36px trend line over a light tint, without axes. Scaled from 0 to its own largest value."
   :props [{:name :values :type "vector of numbers" :doc "Oldest first."}
           {:name :label :type "string" :doc "Accessible name. Without one the sparkline is hidden from screen readers, which is right when the number beside it says enough."}
           {:name :color :type ":accent | :blue | :teal | :orange | :pink | :success" :default "the first series token"}
           {:name :area :type "boolean" :default "true" :doc "false draws the line alone."}
           {:name :zero :type "boolean" :default "true" :doc "false scales from the smallest value instead of 0, for values that move far from zero (a rate between 40 and 50). Use it with :area false: a tint down to a baseline that is not zero would mislead."}
           {:name :curve :type ":smooth | :linear" :default ":smooth"}
           {:name :class :type "string"} {:name :attrs :type "map"}]}
  {:fn "legend"
   :doc "A wrapping row of series names, each after a dot in its color. area-chart adds its own; use this one for charts you compose."
   :props [{:name :items :type "vector of {:label :color :compare}" :doc ":color is one of the chart colors, :compare true gives the muted dot of a comparison series."}
           {:name :class :type "string"} {:name :attrs :type "map"}]}
  {:fn "nice-max" :doc "The axis top for a largest value: rounded up to a round number whose half is round too, at least 4."}
  {:fn "format-number" :doc "A number as text: whole numbers without a decimal, others with one."}
  {:fn "plot-points" :doc "Values as [x y] pairs in a {:w :h :top :low :pad :edges} box."}
  {:fn "line-path" :doc "The SVG path through [x y] pairs, {:curve :smooth | :linear, :h box height}."}
  {:fn "area-path" :doc "A line path closed down to the bottom of the box."}
  {:fn "donut-arcs" :doc "Segments with :dash and :offset for a circle of radius 48."}
  {:fn "pct" :doc "A share of a total in percent with one decimal."}
  {:fn "round1" :doc "A number rounded to one decimal."}
  {:fn "chart-classes" :doc "Class string for a base class and {:color}."}
  {:fn "chart-class-list" :doc "Vector form of chart-classes."}]

 :keyboard
 [["Tab" "Moves through the linked rows of a bar-list. The points of an area-chart are not tab stops."]]

 :accessibility
 ["area-chart carries a visually hidden table of every point with both series, so screen readers get the numbers; the plot, axes and value cards are for sighted reading."
  "The points are focusable by pointer and touch only (tabindex -1): thirty tab stops in a chart would be worse than the table."
  "donut names every segment with its share in the ring's label, and the legend repeats them as text."
  "Give a sparkline a :label when the trend is not said in text next to it."
  "The series color is never the only signal: the comparison line is dashed and the legend names both."]

 :motion
 ["The line and area draw in from the left on first render, rails grow from the left, both over the considered duration."
  "The crosshair, dots and value card fade in over the fast duration; a hovered donut segment thickens."
  "All of it is skipped under reduced motion (the base styles collapse durations)."]

 :responsive
 ["Charts fill their container. The area chart keeps its 200px height; set --chart-h on it for another."
  "On touch devices a tap on a point shows its crosshair and card, a tap elsewhere hides it."
  "The donut's legend wraps under the ring when the container is narrower than about 330px."
  "Axis labels do not thin out by width: pass fewer :axis-label points for a chart that is always narrow."]

 :targets
 {:clj "Static markup; the crosshair needs no script, so it works on server-rendered pages without the runtime."
  :cljs ":class may be a vector. Inline styles are maps of custom properties."
  :squint "Static markup. Inline styles are string-keyed maps of custom properties."}

 :notes-for-ai
 ["Build the point, row and segment maps in the app; the components do no date math and no sorting."
  "Put a chart in a card: (card/card {} (chart/chart {:title ...} (chart/area-chart ...)))."
  "The range picker is a boxed button-group in the chart's :actions (or the page-header's), not tabs."
  "Give charts that are compared with each other the same :max."
  "Spend color with intent: one series color per chart, the comparison stays muted. Do not use status colors for series unless the series is a status."
  "Use :display and :format for units and separators; :value stays a number."]

 :related [:metric :card :button-group :day-grid :progress :table :empty-state]}
